    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Smith Harrington is delighted to present No. 2 St Brigid’s Villas to the market. This three-bedroom terraced residence is ideally situated on Commons Road, just off the N51 Navan to Delvin Road, in a central and convenient location on the west side of Navan town.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 103 sq. m. / 1,108 sq. ft., the property offers well-proportioned accommodation comprising entrance hall, sitting room, dining room, kitchen, back hall, bathroom and three bedrooms.\r\n\r\nThe property benefits from vehicular access to the front, while the rear garden provides additional outdoor space together with a substantial workshop, offering excellent potential for storage, hobbies or a variety of uses.\r\n\r\nBuilt circa 1960, the property is conveniently located close to Navan town centre and a wide range of local amenities including schools, shops, supermarkets, restaurants, sporting facilities and public transport links. The property also enjoys easy access to the N51 and wider road network, providing good connectivity to surrounding towns and Dublin.\r\n\r\nWith its generous accommodation, private rear garden and substantial workshop, No. 2 St Brigid’s Villas offers an excellent opportunity for those seeking a well-located home within Navan."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall 1.77m x 13.58m\r\nBathroom 1.81m x 3.63m\r\nSitting Room 3.63m x 2.79m\r\nDining Room 3.62m x 3.62m\r\nKitchen 3.55m x 2.41m + 2.45m x 3.05m\r\nBack Hall 1.43m x 3.41m\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nLanding 2.27m x 0.93m\r\nBedroom 1 2.67m x 4.60m\r\nBedroom 2 2.92m x 3.52m\r\nBedroom 3 2.60m x 2.55m\r\n\r\nApproximate overall floor area: 103 sq. m. / 1,108 sq. ft.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nThe property is approached via a front garden with vehicular access, providing off-street parking. To the rear is a private garden with a substantial workshop, providing useful additional space for storage, hobbies or a variety of other uses.\r\n\r\nServices\r\nOil fired central heating.        Mains water.             Mains sewerage.\r\n\r\nFixtures & Fittings\r\nProperty being sold as seen. Fixtures, fittings and appliances included in the sale will be detailed as applicable.\r\n\r\nBER Details\r\nBER G No. 119904258\r\n\r\nPerformance Indicator: 524.77 kWh/m²/yr\r\n\r\nTitle\r\nFreehold."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious three-bedroom terraced residence\r\n\r\nApprox. 103 sq. m. / 1,108 sq. ft.\r\n\r\nBuilt circa 1960\r\n\r\nCentral location on the west side of Navan\r\n\r\nConveniently located just off the N51 Navan to Delvin Road\r\n\r\nVehicular access to the front & Private rear garden\r\n\r\nSubstantial rear workshop\r\n\r\nExcellent access to Navan town centre and local amenities\r\n\r\nEasy access to the N51 and surrounding road network\r\n\r\nExcellent potential for a variety of buyers"
      },
